  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 246 AM MDT MON SEP 28 2026\nA flattened ridge, centered over the southwest U.S., will \ndominate the region Thursday through the weekend, with \ntemperatures climbing to 5-10 degrees above normal. A couple of \nweak disturbances may infiltrate the ridge Friday through\nSunday, which would increase cloud cover and bring more \nuncertainty for temperatures. However, precipitation chances \nremain below 10 percent during this time-frame. Early next week,\nmodels favor a strengthening ridge along the West Coast that \nwould support dry, warm, and fair conditions across southeast \nOregon and southwest Idaho.",
